&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Engineering - Developer Experience &amp;amp; Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Awin is seeking an exceptional engineering leader to shape the future of how our engineers build, ship, and operate software at scale. As Head of Engineering – Developer Experience &amp;amp; Platform, you will own the end-to-end developer experience strategy, drive the adoption of AI-native engineering practices, modernise our cloud platform, and lead the teams and tooling that enable Awin&#39;s engineering organisation to work at its best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact leadership role at the intersection of engineering excellence, platform strategy, and AI innovation. You will define and deliver the developer experience (DevEx) vision for Awin, ensuring our engineers have the tools, environments, processes, and culture to be highly productive and deeply satisfied in their work. You will own our platform strategy on AWS, lead FinOps practices, and spearhead the organisation-wide rollout of AI-augmented and agentic development workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as a trusted internal champion for engineers – gathering data-driven insight, translating it into organisation-wide improvements, and working hand-in-hand with engineering leadership, product, and stakeholders to make change happen and allow our Product teams to deliver value to our customers at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right candidate has strong hands-on experience with modern AI-driven software development and building developer-centric cloud platforms at scale. This is a senior but hands-on role within the Engineering organisation, reporting to the Director of Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Tasks &amp;amp; Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Developer Experience Strategy &amp;amp; Tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Awin&#39;s Developer Experience programme – defining the vision, strategy, and roadmap for DevEx improvement across the engineering organisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify friction points, productivity blockers, and systemic inefficiencies through data, qualitative research, and direct engagement with engineering teams, other Heads of Engineering or Engineering Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive organisation-wide improvements to technology, tooling, and engineering processes, building consensus and alignment with key stakeholders across product, engineering, security, and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and track DevEx metrics and KPIs (e.g. DORA metrics, developer satisfaction scores), using them to demonstrate impact and guide investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the developer tools portfolio and associated budgets – evaluating, procuring, and retiring tools to ensure engineers have best-in-class tooling without unnecessary cost or complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic assessment and rollout of new developer tooling, including CI/CD platforms, IDE capabilities, code quality and security tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
